The shopkeeper puts the halwa in a small box.
It is nice red halwa.
"What is the price for this?" I ask.
"Fifty rupees," the shopkeeper says.
I open my bag.
I give exactly fifty rupees.
"Who makes this?" I ask.
"My older brother makes it," he says.
"Your shop is very good," I say.
He smiles happily.
I take the box.
I say thank you to him.
I step out of the shop.
I walk to my apartment.
Anitha is my neighbor.
Halwa is her favorite sweet.
My brother Diego is in Mexico.
His favorite sweet is chocolate.
Today is a calm Sunday.
